{
 "name": "theta-chain-events",
 "notes": "Node 5 of ADR-0265 (H2): earnings-like events labelled from the chain itself, no external calendar. Chain-day features for the sample root (AAPL) at 30 and 90 DTE are rebuilt as in run-theta-chain-features.json, then ChainEventDetector labels a symbol-day an event when the 30-day ATM implied vol falls by at least the frozen threshold between the close of t-1 and the close of t relative to its own trailing 60 sessions and the 30-minus-90-day spread collapses (the underlying's move is output only, never a criterion); event_date is the session whose OPEN holds the move (the crush shows at that session's close); at most one event per symbol per 50 sessions; entry_date = event_date - 3 sessions, exit_date = event_date + 1 session. THE DETECTOR IS A RETROSPECTIVE LABELLER, NOT A LIVE SIGNAL: the entry date precedes the detection date, so an entry three sessions before the event is known only ex post. The thresholds are params of the node, frozen in this document, chosen on AAPL 2016-2019 dates only (ADR-0265 Amendment 4); the calibrate node re-scores a grid against the labelled AAPL announcement dates 2016-2019 (rows and labels from 2020-01-01 are dropped and counted before scoring, so the grid never sees 2020+) and only REPORTS: it applies nothing. DEVELOPMENT YEARS ONLY: end_before 2021-01-01 on every node and only 2016-2020 dates are read into the nodes, so the validation years 2021-2025 are not run until the one pre-registered validation run. READ-ONLY on /home/russell/data/thetadata/options-tested. Run from children/index_options: python -m dskit.pipeline run configs/run-theta-chain-events.json --asof 2025-12-31.",
 "outputs": {
  "run_root": "/home/russell/data/index_options/theta-research-20261012/chain-events",
  "notes": "A new directory beside the other research runs; nothing is written under /home/russell/data/thetadata. Excluded from the identity hash."
 },
